{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["The 'arov — I say that they are a species of wolves called ערוב, because their way is to prey at night, as it is written (Jeremiah 5:6) זאב ערבות ישדדם, and it is written (Zephaniah 3:3) זאבי ערב לא גרמו לבקר. And just as one says מאודם אדום, so they say — [variant reading: מאודם אדום — from depth, deep]. From ערב, ערוב —Old French [טרינ\"ד in Old French], for the wolf is ערוב because it goes about in the evening. 'Deep' is the noun; 'deep' [the adjective] is the action. And likewise אדום — 'black.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "The Hebrew appears textually corrupt in several places: נו\"י and עמוק/עמק are likely scribal errors, and the sequence 'והמעשה קרוי עמוק' is uncertain. The lemma לא גרמו לבקר follows Zephaniah 3:3. Translation is hyper-literal to preserve the difficulty."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:40:50.918747669Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}